 "short_name": "George",
 "_doc": "TWO STATEMENT LAYOUTS in one folder, both genuine George municipal tax invoices, fingerprinted on George's OWN VAT registration 4630193664 + the masthead 'George Municipality'. NEVER fingerprint on 4680101146 - that is Telkom's own 'Client VAT Number / VAT Reg Number' and it is printed on bills from 16 other folders in this tree. No cbreexcellerate address is used.\nLAYOUT A - legacy detail ('Computer Generated Tax Invoice For : <Month> - <Year>'), files GEO_OCT 2025 (8 pages) and GEO_NOV 2025 (4 pages). Full per-meter detail. Every charge block is\n    Reading dates: Cur dd/mm/yyyy Prev dd/mm/yyyy (n days)\n    Cur <reading> Prev <reading> Cons <qty> KWH|KVA|KL\n    Meter <no> [(Estimate)]\n    <qty> x <rate> = <amount>\n    Tariff: <tariff name>\n  and the ex-VAT / VAT / incl-VAT money TRIPLE sits at the END of the block in the Oct file but in the MIDDLE (right after 'Dwelling Units') in the Nov file, so amounts are taken from the '<qty> x <rate> = <amount>' line, which is in the same place in both. Every pattern that walks from a Cons line to a Tariff line uses the tempered token (?:(?!Reading dates:)[\\s\\S])*? so it can never run past its own block into the next meter (blocks are separated by whole repeated page headers/footers, which the guard also survives). Oct spaces its thousands (R 32 437.91) and writes dates dd-mm-yyyy; Nov commas them (R 29,281.95) and writes yyyy-mm-dd. Nov's PDF also kerns words apart - 'Dw elling', 'Netw ork', 'Sew er', 'Ow ner', 'Swif t' - so 'Netw ?ork' is spelled defensively and no pattern relies on 'Dwelling'.\n  TOU tariff 3B: 'Time Of Use Peak/Standard/Off Peak 3B' are the kWh bands; 'Time Of Use Basic And Kva 3B' on a KVA meter is the MAXIMUM DEMAND charge (-> demand_kva/demand_r) while the same wording with 'Basic:' and no readings is the fixed monthly service charge (-> other); 'Time Of Use Netw ork Access 3B' is the NOTIFIED maximum demand, a constant 194.407 kVA (-> nmd); 'Reactive Energy Charge' is billed as KVA on the statement but is really kvarh (-> other); 'Elec Cons 3Phase' are three small non-TOU kWh meters on the same account (-> geo_a_flat_*, other).\n  Reading registers self-check: summing Cur and Prev over EVERY 'Cons ... KWH' block and subtracting gives exactly the summed Cons (Oct 78 588.000, Nov 76 786.360).\n  total_ex_vat_r is the INDEPENDENTLY PRINTED electricity 'Sub Total', so reconcile on Layout A is a real check, not a circular one.\nLAYOUT B - new ERP summary ('Tax Invoice Number 2026NN/[number removed]', masthead 'VAT No. 4630193664 George Municipality / P.O. Box 19, George, 6530'), files GEO_DEC 2025 and GEO_JAN..APR 2026, 2 pages each. IT PRINTS NO ELECTRICITY CONSUMPTION AT ALL: no readings, no kWh, no kVA, no TOU band split, no reading dates. All that exists is the per-service ledger table (Opening | Receipts | Billed Amount | Billed VAT | Interest | Journals | Closing) with rows 'Electricity Basic' and 'Electricity Metered', plus an 'Electricity Details:' table at the foot that lists only Type / Tariff code / Meter Number / Connection Size (TOUPM TOUSD TOUSM TOUOS TOUSA REACT + three '1508' meters). Blank kWh / band / reading columns on Layout B are the bill's silence, not a missed regex. On Layout B total_ex_vat_r is the sum of the two printed Electricity rows and other_r is the same two figures, so reconcile there IS circular - declared openly. The genuine Layout B checks are (a) elec Billed VAT == 15% of elec Billed Amount and (b) the eight service Billed Amounts == the printed 'Total' row. On Layout A the genuine check is the five section Sub Totals == 'Total Levies for the Month'.\nSizes are artwork, not scans: GEO_DEC 2025 is 3.2 MB yet 2 pages / 6 907 chars of real text. All 7 statements have a text layer (read_pdf ocr=auto reports ocr:False scanned:False) - nothing needs Tesseract.\nSIBLING DOCUMENT TYPE: the same folder holds six 'Amptera _ George _ bills.view_saved_bill_Telkom_HV_<Mon>2026.pdf' browser print-outs of the Amptera open-access billing portal. They are NOT municipal statements, so reject_if_text disqualifies this profile on them and profile 'george_amptera' (same short_name 'George') owns them.",
